e Airbyte. This isn't a keep-the-lights-on role. You'll make real tradeoffs between engineering velocity, customer-facing reliability, and long-term architecture every week, and you'll help define how AI transforms the way we build and operate software.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role combines people leadership, technical strategy, operational excellence, and platform thinking. You'll help define how engineering works at Airbyte - not just what we build.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and grow a team of Platform Engineers, Fullstack Engineers, and SREs. Recruit engineers who understand that infrastructure decisions are product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the reliability and operational health of Airbyte's production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the roadmap for Airbyte's platform: infrastructure, CI/CD, deployment automation, observability, internal tooling, and the product surfaces built on top of them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Invest in and drive adoption of AI-powered workflows for debugging, release validation, infrastructure management, and developer productivity, moving past experimentation into real operational leverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident response, run blameless postmortems, and ensure systemic fixes follow every outage. Continuously reduce operational toil through automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build leverage: a week-long task this year should take ten minutes next year.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Success Metrics:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineers deploy with confidence and ship faster quarter over 